Task 1: Choose a Business Domain
Selected Domain: Finance

The finance industry handles large volumes of customer transactions daily. Detecting fraudulent activities quickly and accurately is critical to reducing financial losses and protecting customer trust.

Task 2: Define the Business Problem
Problem Statement

Financial institutions face increasing challenges in detecting fraudulent transactions in real time. Traditional rule-based systems often fail to identify sophisticated fraud patterns and generate a high number of false alerts.

The goal is to design an AI-powered fraud detection system that can automatically identify suspicious financial transactions using machine learning and neural networks.

Stakeholders / Users
Banks and financial institutions
Fraud investigation teams
Customers
Risk management departments
Regulatory authorities
Current Traditional Process

Most banks currently use:

Rule-based fraud detection systems
Manual verification by fraud analysts
Static threshold-based alerts

Example:

Transaction amount exceeds a limit
Multiple failed login attempts
Transactions from unusual locations
Limitations of Current Process
High false positive rate
Slow manual investigation
Difficulty detecting new fraud patterns
Limited scalability
Delayed response to fraudulent activity
Customer dissatisfaction due to unnecessary transaction blocking
Task 3: Identify the AI Task Type
Selected AI Task Type: Classification

The problem is treated as a binary classification task where transactions are classified as:

Fraudulent
Legitimate
Why Classification is Suitable

The system needs to predict whether a transaction belongs to one of two predefined classes. Neural network classification models are effective at learning hidden patterns from historical transaction data and identifying suspicious activities.

