Task 5: Model Recommendation
Recommended Model: Feed-Forward Neural Network (FNN)
Alternative Advanced Models
LSTM for sequential transaction behavior
Autoencoders for anomaly detection
Transformer-based fraud analysis systems
Why Feed-Forward Neural Network is Appropriate

A Feed-Forward Neural Network works well because:

Transaction data is primarily structured
The model can learn nonlinear fraud patterns
It handles large datasets efficiently
It improves prediction accuracy compared to rule-based systems
Proposed Model Architecture
Input Layer
    ↓
Hidden Layer 1 (ReLU)
    ↓
Hidden Layer 2 (ReLU)
    ↓
Dropout Layer
    ↓
Output Layer (Sigmoid)
Model Processing Flow
Transaction data enters the system
Features are normalized and encoded
Neural network processes transaction patterns
Fraud probability score is generated
Suspicious transactions are flagged for review
