Task 7: Responsible AI Considerations
Bias in Data

Historical fraud data may contain:

Geographic bias
Customer demographic bias
Device usage bias

Mitigation:

Balanced training data
Bias testing during evaluation
Fairness monitoring
Incorrect Predictions

Risks:

Genuine customers may be blocked
Fraudulent transactions may pass undetected

Mitigation:

Human review system
Confidence threshold tuning
Ensemble validation methods
Privacy Concerns

Sensitive financial data must be protected.

Mitigation:

Data encryption
Access control mechanisms
Compliance with GDPR and banking regulations
Secure data storage
Over-Reliance on AI

Employees should not fully depend on automated predictions.

Mitigation:

Human-in-the-loop system
Analyst approval workflows
Explainable AI dashboards
Impact on Users

Potential impacts:

Account freezing
Delayed payments
Customer frustration

Mitigation:

Fast verification channels
Transparent communication
Appeal and dispute process
